## 2. Problem Analysis — Why Current Fork Model Fails

Your current approach (`plan_approach_a_fork.md`) duplicates the **entire codebase** for each institute. This has severe scaling issues:

| Problem | Current Fork Model | Proposed SaaS Model |
|:---|:---|:---|
| Adding a new institute | Copy codebase + new Supabase project (~55 min manual) | Click "Add Institute" in admin panel (~2 min automated) |
| Bug fix or feature update | Manually apply to ALL 25 repos ❌ | Deploy once → all 25 institutes get the update ✅ |
| Code maintenance | 25 separate repos × 12 files per branding change = 300 changes | 1 repo, 1 config table in DB, 0 code changes |
| Infrastructure cost | 25 Vercel projects + 25 Supabase projects | 1 App + 1 RDS instance (25 schemas inside) |
| Monthly cost (estimated) | ₹50,000–1,00,000/month | ₹8,000–15,000/month |
| Developer onboarding | Must understand 25 different repos | Single codebase, single pattern |

> **Verdict:** The fork model is unsustainable at 25+ institutes. A proper multi-tenant SaaS is the only path forward.

