## 3. Multi-Tenancy Architecture — Deep Dive

### 3.1 Three Multi-Tenancy Models Compared

| Model | Data Isolation | Cost | Complexity | Our Decision |
|:---|:---|:---|:---|:---|
| **Shared DB, Shared Schema** (Row-Level Security) | Low — `WHERE tenant_id = ?` on every query | ₹₹ | Low | ❌ Risk of data leaks |
| **Shared DB, Separate Schemas** ⭐ | High — each tenant has own PostgreSQL schema | ₹₹₹ | Medium | ✅ **RECOMMENDED** |
| **Separate Databases** | Highest — fully isolated DBs | ₹₹₹₹₹ | High | ❌ Too expensive for 25 |

### 3.2 Why Schema-per-Tenant is the Sweet Spot

```
Single PostgreSQL RDS Instance (Amazon RDS)
├── public schema           → Master Database (tenants, billing, super admin)
├── tenant_institute1       → Institute 1's complete data (students, courses, etc.)
├── tenant_bce              → BCE's complete data
├── tenant_xyzuniversity    → XYZ University's complete data
└── ... (up to 100 schemas in a single RDS instance)
```

**Benefits:**
- ✅ **True data isolation** — `SET search_path TO tenant_bce` before any query
- ✅ **Single RDS bill** — no need for 25 AWS database instances
- ✅ **Easy backup/restore** per tenant — `pg_dump --schema=tenant_bce`
- ✅ **Easy tenant removal** — `DROP SCHEMA tenant_bce CASCADE`
- ✅ **Same Prisma schema** — apply identical migrations to all tenant schemas
- ✅ **Connection pooling** — PgBouncer shares connections across all tenants

### 3.3 Request Lifecycle (How It Works)

```
┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│  Student visits: bce.edusaas.com/dashboard                      │
│     ↓                                                           │
│  Next.js Middleware → extracts subdomain "bce"                  │
│     ↓                                                           │
│  Master DB lookup → SELECT schema_name FROM tenants             │
│                     WHERE slug = 'bce' AND status = 'active'    │
│     ↓                                                           │
│  Returns: schema_name = "tenant_bce"                            │
│     ↓                                                           │
│  Prisma Client → SET search_path TO tenant_bce                  │
│     ↓                                                           │
│  All queries scoped to tenant_bce schema automatically          │
│     ↓                                                           │
│  Response returned to student (only sees BCE data)               │
└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

