## 10. Security & Data Isolation

### 10.1 Security Checklist

| Area | Implementation |
|:---|:---|
| **Tenant Isolation** | PostgreSQL schema-level isolation + `SET search_path` enforced per request |
| **Cross-tenant leaks** | Middleware validates tenant context; DB queries never reference other schemas |
| **Authentication** | bcrypt password hashing + JWT tokens with `tenantId` claim |
| **Authorization** | RBAC middleware checks `role` + `tenantId` on every protected route |
| **API Security** | Rate limiting per tenant (Redis-based), CORS restricted to tenant domains |
| **Data Encryption** | TLS in transit (CloudFront + RDS), AES-256 encryption at rest (RDS) |
| **SQL Injection** | Parameterized queries via Drizzle ORM (never raw string interpolation) |
| **File Isolation** | S3 bucket policy: tenants can only read/write within their `tenants/{slug}/` prefix |
| **Super Admin** | 2FA enforced, audit log for all admin actions |
| **Backup** | Automated RDS snapshots + per-schema `pg_dump` for tenant-level restore |

### 10.2 Tenant Suspension Flow

```
Stripe payment fails (3 retries over 7 days)
    ↓
Webhook sets tenant.billing_status = 'suspended'
    ↓
Middleware detects 'suspended' status
    ↓
All routes for that tenant redirect to /suspended page
    ↓
Suspended page shows: "Your subscription has expired. Please contact admin."
    ↓
Data is PRESERVED (not deleted). Super admin can reactivate.
    ↓
After 90 days of suspension → Super admin can choose to archive (pg_dump) and DROP SCHEMA
```

